<p>Seems like a kind of cliche idea, but you really ran with it and made it interesting, so it's a +1 from me.</p>
<p>Couple of small notes though,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Analysis of footage revealed that the measurement appearing on the reflected version of the thermocouple was at the expected temperature, not matching its counterpart in reality.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's unclear what you mean by &quot;expected&quot;. Do you mean it matched the real thermocouple, or it matched the temperature of the flames it produced?</p>
<p>Also, the containment procedures seem a bit unlikely. Surely an independent generator is preferable to putting it in a room with a skylight? 1, because skylights won't help much at night, and 2, it harms the security of the containment.</p>

