														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2487971">
									

<p>You might specify the skylight as a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_tube">light tube</a> system- those collect light from outside, and pipe it through an internally-reflective tube to the interior of a building. They have the advantage of being able to use lenses to concentrate the light from a broad collection area into a single point- sort of like a lighthouse in reverse, or a telescope that doesn't create an image. A backup generator would still be a good idea, but passive lighting doesn't run out of fuel and works as long as it's not a new moon on a cloudy night.</p>
<p>Actually use them in prisons for the above reasons, and because you can't break out through a fiber optic cable attached to the center of a collection dish inside a one-way mirror.</p>

							</div>

								
